The Companion memory wiring for the composition root.

`main.ts` is owned by several concurrent branches at once, so this branch ships its wiring here
rather than editing the file, exactly as `companion-question-main.patch` did before it.

Applies to web/packages/app/src/main.ts at c88202901ef5286ed9008eaed63cce6929af6c67.

    git apply docs/patches/companion-memory-main.patch

Without it, `mountCompanion` still compiles and still runs: `persistedMemory` and `rememberAnswer`
are optional, and a host that has not opted in gets the behaviour it had, an empty memory and no
write-back. That is deliberate rather than a courtesy. A default that half worked would be a
Companion claiming to remember and quietly not.

Verified applied on this branch: web typecheck, dependency-cruiser and vitest all pass with it,
and section 7 of docs/companion-question.md is this patch applied and driven in a browser.

